/**
 * @defgroup kfsw_platform K-FSW Platform
 * @brief Zephyr-backed platform lifecycle and hardware capabilities.
 *
 * Platform APIs expose mechanisms needed by services and the application
 * without creating a replacement hardware abstraction layer.
 *
 * @defgroup kfsw_platform_time Time
 * @ingroup kfsw_platform
 * @brief Monotonic elapsed-time readings for scheduling and measurements.
 *
 * See kfsw_time_monotonic_ms() and kfsw_time_monotonic_us(). These readings
 * are local elapsed time, not synchronized spacecraft time.
 *
 * @defgroup kfsw_platform_storage Storage
 * @ingroup kfsw_platform
 * @brief LittleFS backend lifecycle and capacity reporting.
 *
 * Initialize with kfsw_storage_init(), mount with kfsw_storage_mount(), and
 * query state with kfsw_storage_get_info(). Services use Zephyr filesystem
 * calls after kfsw_storage_is_ready() reports true.
 *
 * @defgroup kfsw_platform_reset Reset
 * @ingroup kfsw_platform
 * @brief Hardware reset-cause access.
 *
 * kfsw_platform_get_reset_cause() reads and clears the platform reset flags.
 *
 * @defgroup kfsw_comms K-FSW Communications
 * @brief CSP lifecycle, routing, and transport status.
 *
 * Communications owns libcsp integration and packet-routing lifecycle. Client
 * services use the public K-FSW APIs instead of owning routers or transports.
 *
 * @defgroup kfsw_comms_csp CSP
 * @ingroup kfsw_comms
 * @brief libcsp initialization, route inspection, and ping operations.
 *
 * The application calls kfsw_csp_init() before registering CSP services and
 * calls kfsw_csp_start() once to start the router thread.
 *
 * @defgroup kfsw_comms_uart UART / KISS
 * @ingroup kfsw_comms
 * @brief Independently configured UART transports and end-to-end test support.
 *
 * kfsw_uart_visit() reports every configured interface and its counters;
 * kfsw_uart_test_peer() verifies and reports the UART selected for a node.
 *
 * @defgroup kfsw_services K-FSW Services
 * @brief Reusable software services composed by the K-FSW application.
 *
 * @defgroup kfsw_services_boot Boot
 * @ingroup kfsw_services
 * @brief Stable boot and readiness markers for operators and automation.
 *
 * @defgroup kfsw_services_logging Logging
 * @ingroup kfsw_services
 * @brief Runtime log filtering and compile-time-aware logging calls.
 *
 * @defgroup kfsw_services_param Parameters
 * @ingroup kfsw_services
 * @brief Local tables and persistence with optional remote CSP access.
 *
 * Initialize the local table with kfsw_param_init(). The application restores
 * persistence independently of CSP. When CONFIG_KFSW_PARAM_CSP is enabled,
 * kfsw_param_server_start() exposes the same table through the CSP adapter.
 *
 * @defgroup kfsw_services_ftp FTP
 * @ingroup kfsw_services
 * @brief Sandboxed file transfer over CSP/RDP with CRC32 validation.
 *
 * kfsw_ftp_init() prepares storage. kfsw_ftp_start() binds the server after
 * storage and the CSP router are ready. PUT and GET stream bounded chunks and
 * atomically commit received files.
 */
